---
description: Preserve the approved illustrated travel diorama across data generation and package loading
globs: labs/travel/**
alwaysApply: false
---

- Follow `labs/travel/AGENTS.md` and `visual-style.js`.
- Keep the approved pastel diorama, original landmark models and air-arc-v1 arrows.
- Generated itineraries may select known place IDs and order stops; they must not
  generate CSS, shaders, materials, model code or replacement arrow styles.
- Data packages are geometry and itinerary inputs, never executable theme code.
- Pin the renderer and its dependencies, and verify content hashes before use.
- Changing cache availability, destinations or detail level must not select a new style.
- Change the style version only after an explicit user-requested visual change;
  preserve older content-addressed assets when deploying updates.
- Check Paris and Shanghai, screen and export, flat and height modes. Reopening
  the same data with the same camera must reproduce its appearance. Never promise
  byte-identical pixels across different GPUs, browsers or fonts.
